h(2, id: "callouts") { 13. Callouts }

p {
    Admonition block. Body is prose.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
callout { Defaults to note. }
callout(type: "warning") { Check the heading level. }
!}

p {
    code{type} is a string. Matching is case-insensitive.
}

table {
    row(header: true) {
        cell { type }
        cell { Also accepted }
    }
    row {
        cell { note }
        cell { info }
    }
    row {
        cell { tip }
        cell { hint }
    }
    row {
        cell { warning }
        cell { caution }
    }
    row {
        cell { danger }
        cell { error }
    }
}

p {
    Any other string is a parse error. Omitted type is note. code{title}
    replaces the default heading text.
}

codeblock(lang: "text") {!
callout(type: "tip", title: "Watch mode") { Run code{docup watch index.du}. }
!}

callout(type: "note") {
    Semantic errors are reported with file, line, and column. The compiler
    prints the source line and a caret.
}

callout(type: "tip") {
    Put examples in codeblock raw scopes so the sample is not parsed as DocUP.
}

callout(type: "warning") {
    Heading levels outside 1 through 6 fail semantic analysis, not parsing. The
    tokens are valid; the values are not.
}

callout(type: "danger") {
    include cycles and missing include files fail before semantic analysis. The
    error is reported against the include statement.
}
